	(text "Datasheet notes on antenna ladder:\n\nC501 (C6 in datasheet) grounding must ONLY be connected to Pin32 (VSS_PA)\non same layer.\n\nPin32 must ONLY be connected to Pin49 (VSS_PAD) underneath the IC package.\n\nC502 (C9 in datasheet) MUST be isolated from ALL ground layers except bottom ground layer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.202 117.856 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "89cc8851-a19f-46e3-b9aa-605b42542086")
	)
	(text "nRF54L10 - as per datasheet\n\nI don't do RF. So I just follow the datasheet as closely as possible."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.832 174.244 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "90c1d055-9122-4ece-a76e-adc0f1f237ad")
	)
	(text "The mouser pdf datasheet has a 10nF cap each on DECA and DECRF, but then the (updated?)\nannoying html datasheet at nordicsemi.com replaced the DECRF one with 2.2nF.\n\nAnd on the CSP47 version it became 3.9pF instead - and *both* are marked DNM, and instead there\nare two 2.2uF capacitors with another ferrite in between them.\n\nAargh. \n\nAside: Why do the Nordic people say \"DNM\" (for \"do not mount\") when everybody else says \"DNP\"\n(\"do not place\")?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cdfaf9a2-2b4a-4698-b92a-83dde0f83654")
	)
	(text_box "3.3V bypass capacitors"
